meta { name: Record a view, type: http, seq: 1 }
post { url: {{publicBase}}/views, body: json, auth: none }
headers { X-Tenant-Key: {{techTenantKey}} }
body:json { { "articleId": "{{articleId}}", "referrer": "https://l.facebook.com/", "language": "en-GB", "screen": "1440x900" } }
docs {
  What each site's /api/views route calls. 404 for unknown / unpublished /
  other-tenant ids. Counted in article_views first, then forwarded to Umami
  fire-and-forget — Umami being down changes nothing here.

  The sites also send X-Reader-Ip and X-Reader-User-Agent (the reader's, from
  the site server) for geo/device/bot detection. Never stored or logged.

  Separate Kong service (public-write-api). If this 404s with "no Route
  matched", Kong is running a stale config: re-render and restart it.
}
